# Project Rules

- Read `AGENT.md` before planning or editing. It is the project-wide source of truth.
- Build a server-rendered Django administration application with progressive enhancement.
- Use Django templates/forms, HTMX, Alpine.js, Tailwind CSS, `docxtpl`, and narrowly scoped `python-docx` work.
- Preserve the core workflows: authenticated access, record list/search, validated data entry, and authorized `.docx` export for VDS document types.
- Keep the dashboard responsive and framework-agnostic; do not couple product design to Filament.
- Make the smallest coherent change and follow established repository patterns.
- Never move validation, permissions, or workflow truth exclusively to the browser.
- Do not introduce an SPA framework, API layer, task queue, cache, or new infrastructure without a measured requirement.
- Treat legal-case data, draft payloads, and generated documents as sensitive.
- Update tests with behavior changes and run the repository-configured checks before reporting completion.
- Never claim a check passed unless it was actually run successfully.
- Ask before changing legal wording, retention rules, authorization boundaries, stable payload/template keys, or destructive migrations.
